{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01485",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.6,
      "end_seconds": 2.06,
      "duration_seconds": 1.46,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 3.13,
      "end_seconds": 7.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.43,
      "text": "Not at all, please sit. What seems to be wrong?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 9.19,
      "end_seconds": 29.87,
      "duration_seconds": 20.68,
      "text": "Mainly burning when I pass urine. There's a couple of other things, but that's the main one. I did try to ignore it for a while. I told myself I'd wait and see, and here I am."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 31.07,
      "end_seconds": 37.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.22,
      "text": "when was the first time you noticed it? It helps to be thorough at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 38.43,
      "end_seconds": 40.37,
      "duration_seconds": 1.94,
      "text": "Probably ten days. Yeah."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 40.61,
      "end_seconds": 51.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.66,
      "text": "yes, carry on tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 52.49,
      "end_seconds": 64.35,
      "duration_seconds": 11.86,
      "text": "Actually, it happens once or twice a day. It settles a little with drinking water. And I've been going to the toilet often as well."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.69,
      "end_seconds": 80.89,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "I'll do your observations first."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 91.82,
      "end_seconds": 94.17,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Keep your arm relaxed for me..."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 113.86,
      "end_seconds": 123.17,
      "duration_seconds": 9.31,
      "text": "Okay: pulse is 86 beats a minute, respiratory rate 15, temperature 36.8. And saturation 99 percent, blood pressure 113 over 80."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 124.88,
      "end_seconds": 126.3,
      "duration_seconds": 1.42,
      "text": "Is that okay?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 128.21,
      "end_seconds": 132.47,
      "duration_seconds": 4.26,
      "text": "They help me see the whole picture, more shortly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 134.36,
      "end_seconds": 137.08,
      "duration_seconds": 2.72,
      "text": "Let's move on to the examination."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 138.08,
      "end_seconds": 140.95,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "stay as you are for a moment"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 152.26,
      "end_seconds": 157.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with slight tenderness just above the pubic bone."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.04,
      "end_seconds": 168.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Yeah, no problem."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.09,
      "end_seconds": 178.38,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "All finished, thank you. Have you noticed blood in the urine, vaginal discharge or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 180.26,
      "end_seconds": 184.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.97,
      "text": "Uh, no, not a single one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 185.49,
      "end_seconds": 187.34,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "Nothing like back pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.72,
      "end_seconds": 191.67,
      "duration_seconds": 2.95,
      "text": "No, none, no back pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 192.11,
      "end_seconds": 198.3,
      "duration_seconds": 6.19,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Have you noticed any weakness, or anything odd with your balance?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 200.02,
      "end_seconds": 202.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "No, nothing like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 203.72,
      "end_seconds": 206.23,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Now some background about your lifestyle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.05,
      "end_seconds": 222.57,
      "duration_seconds": 10.52,
      "text": "I live with my elderly mother. I'm a hairdresser, on my feet all day. I grab fast food at lunch most days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.66,
      "end_seconds": 238.49,
      "duration_seconds": 2.83,
      "text": "Any past operations I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 239.14,
      "end_seconds": 247.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.59,
      "text": "I had a bunion operation six years ago. I just want to get back to normal, really."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 249.31,
      "end_seconds": 256.41,
      "duration_seconds": 7.1,
      "text": "Can you list what you take, tablets, creams or inhalers? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 257.58,
      "end_seconds": 260.52,
      "duration_seconds": 2.94,
      "text": "Tiotropium inhaler, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.88,
      "end_seconds": 274.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.8,
      "text": "Alright, what conditions have you been treated for in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 275.58,
      "end_seconds": 277.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.92,
      "text": "COPD, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.87,
      "end_seconds": 287.61,
      "duration_seconds": 8.74,
      "text": "I follow let me tell you where I've got to i think we're dealing with an uncomplicated urinary infection at this stage"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 288.3,
      "end_seconds": 290.45,
      "duration_seconds": 2.15,
      "text": "is this serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.87,
      "end_seconds": 310.4,
      "duration_seconds": 18.53,
      "text": "nothing I've seen today points to an emergency it looks like an uncomplicated urinary infection i'll start you on nitrofurantoin, 100 milligrams, twice a day, three days it's for urinary infection is there anything you'd like me to go over again?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 311.39,
      "end_seconds": 314.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Good, thanks, I'll see you then."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.32,
      "end_seconds": 318.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.97,
      "text": "Have a good day."
    }
  ]
}